    "result_text": "The full test suite passes. All 3 test files are accounted for (`AcceptanceBase` is abstract, `AuditLogCapture` is a helper, `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class), and its `coreComputesDisplayName` test passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required that a created owner return `displayName` formatted exactly as `LastName, FirstName` from the stored names. Two changes implement this:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `displayName` string property to the `Owner` response schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` now carries the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a MapStruct mapping that computes it from the stored names:\n   ```java\n   @Mapping(target = \"displayName\",\n       expression = \"java(owner.getLastName() + \\\", \\\" + owner.getFirstName())\")\n   OwnerDto toOwnerDto(Owner owner);\n   ```\n\nBecause the OfficeFloor responders (`RespondWithOwnerCreated`, `RespondWithOwner`) already map the stored `Owner` entity through `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto`, the `displayName` is derived from the persisted `lastName`/`firstName` and appears on both the create response and the `GET /api/owners/{id}` read-back the test asserts against. `BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`.",
